  "question": {
    "text": "The chord $P Q$ of the parabola $y^2=x$, where one end $P$ of the chord is at point $(4,-2)$, is perpendicular to the axis of the parabola. Then the slope of the normal at $Q$ is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "qwm0k",
      "text": "\n$-4$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "EzAxl",
      "text": "\n$-\\frac{1}{4}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "Aup4L",
      "text": "\n4\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2oYzF",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{1}{4}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Point $P$ is $(4,-2)$ and $P Q \\perp x$-axis So, $Q=(4,2)$\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/uIx6mmuTF_FGALU_1iwHjbKu8dhu8y8PzUFSjJuNmZQ.original.fullsize.png\"><br>\nEquation of tangent at $(4,2)$ is\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& y y_1=\\frac{1}{2}\\left(x+x_1\\right) \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow 2 y=\\frac{1}{2}(x+2) \\Rightarrow 4 y=x+2 \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow y=\\frac{x}{4}+\\frac{1}{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nSo, slope of tangent $=\\frac{1}{4}$\n$\\therefore$ Slope of normal $=-4$",
    "image": null
  },
